WEBVTT

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:32.630
We're just acting! 
You didn't have to actually do it!

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:33.470
Huh?

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.830
Ah, but...

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.600
It was in the script...

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:41.970
Was it?

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:48.610
Where?

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:51.610
Here.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:55.240
<b>That's 
a must!</b>

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:55.240
<b>*Do it
 for real</b>

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.240
It's handwritten.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:58.490
It wasn't me!

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.990
So... someone wrote it into the script?

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:05.040
But the scripts were just handed out today.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:09.630
I got mine from Komori-kun...

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:23.810
Ow...

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.150
Don't you run away.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.570
Yeah, but... Come on...

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:38.490
<b>Gokuraku   Komori     Prince:</b>

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.990
Komori.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.200
Komori.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:37.740
Komori.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:43.490
<b>Prince:
Gokuraku   Komori</b>

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:43.490
<b>Princess:
Ikkaku   Mitama   Kimihara</b>

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.570
That's it.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:43.620
Okay, so the prince will be 
played by Komori Makoto-kun.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:44.500
All right!

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.160
Yes!

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.620
Komori-kun, sit down.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.590
Sit down right now.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:55.960
Here's your script.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:01:58.680
Oh... Thank you.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.100
Let's knock 'em dead.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.720
Y-Yeah...

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.090
What the heck? That creep!

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:10.980
Hey, Komori. 
Don't forget my foie gras roll.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:11.980
Hey! You idiot!

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:23.160
So, because Komori-kun cheated through 
the use of bribery and coercion,

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.120
he is dismissed from the prince's role.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:29.250
The prince will now be played 
by Gokuraku Nozomi-san.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.750
That's kind of a pain, too...

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:38.760
I was supposed to play the prince...

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:42.220
You totally brought this upon yourself.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.260
And you, Hime...

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.720
Did you plan to actually kiss Komori?

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:47.600
Huh?

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:50.060
Well, I, uh...

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.770
I thought it'd be fine if it 
was with you, Nozomi-chan.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:56.610
Hot and heavy, eh?

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.280
Sounds like love!

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.400
What the heck...?

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:04.620
All right, don't get so worked 
up over a simple kiss.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.410
Time to continue with rehearsal.

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.750
Oh? A simple kiss?

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.660
Wh-Wh-Wh...

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.250
In any case, it doesn't count if 
it's between friends, right?

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.550
Back to rehearsal!

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:18.760
You heard her.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.630
Still, sorry about that.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:23.890
You don't have to apologize for that.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.380
Whew, I'm beat.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:35.690
Why does our class have to do a play?

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:37.980
A chorus or something would've been easier.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:41.030
Probably because our class 
president is such a go-getter.

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:44.530
It's kinda fun, though, isn't it?

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.080
Is it?

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.330
Hey, you got to kiss Hime, didn't you?

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:52.080
Oh? Didn't expect that reaction.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.290
Anyway, you're surprisingly 
good at acting, Hime.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.050
Oh, yeah...

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:01.290
I played a princess in middle school, too.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.180
And elementary school...

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:05.050
And kindergarten.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.350
And in your nursery, too?

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.140
Oh... Yeah!

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:11.420
I was my daddy's princess, too!

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:13.850
Because of my name, I guess...

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:16.480
Uh, no, it's gotta be your 
looks and behavior.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.320
I'd be fine with just being Passerby A.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.320
<i>What's this?
 Is she really bragging that easily?</i>

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.410
'Sup?

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.880
Things are really coming along.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.670
The costumes are mostly done, 
too, so try them on.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.970
Wow!

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:47.970
This is great!

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:49.810
Yep, that was hard work.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.470
It's set in medieval Scandinavia, right?

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:54.270
So a centaur princess is actually 
historically impossible.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.980
It might have a shot in Russia, though,

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.810
so I used Russia, Central Asia, and the 
Near and Middle East as references,

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.860
with a bit of Baroque 
influence in the lace.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:01.900
I guess you'd call it Bourbon style?

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.780
But the story's set in medieval Scandinavia, 
and I don't know the playwright at all,

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:03.780
That's gonna go on for a while.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.910
She's a real nerd when it comes 
to history and costumes.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.360
so I guess it doesn't have to 
be historically accurate,

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:08.490
but that's exactly why I want 
the details to be realistic!

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.410
But you know...

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:15.290
I thought I made it on the large side,
 but it's pretty tight.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:16.040
Huh?!

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.630
Oh, that looks great! Way to go, me!

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.130
Hey, Mitama!

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:26.220
Can we bring the scenery in?

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.340
Oh, sure. Please do.

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:29.930
All right, bring it in!

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.100
Got it!

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.170
Fujimoto-kun, may I?

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:56.160
I'd like more braces on these.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.920
We tested it out. It'll be fine.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:02.180
No one can be heavier than Nekomi, right?

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:03.710
Uh...

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:06.620
Anyway...

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:10.430
You never know what could happen, 
so just reinforce it.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:11.600
All right.

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:15.770
Okay, now that we have the scenery in here,

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.690
let's run through the whole thing,
 with feeling.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:21.650
Oh... and of course, don't do <i>that</i>.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:24.780
Okay, begin!

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:27.900
This is the one with the real kiss, right?

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:28.990
Seriously?

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.240
Hey, aren't you going to kiss?

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:38.790
They will not.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.750
Aw...

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.800
Now we've got weird rumors going around...

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.140
<b>School
 Recital</b>

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:03.940
They're finished.

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.850
Okay, let's carry in our set.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.780
It's our turn! I'm getting nervous!

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.450
Easy, girl.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.240
Be careful with that.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:18.080
It'll be fine!

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:22.880
<i>Next is Class 1-1's play,
</i>A Dream Under the Midnight Sun<i>.</i>

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:01.410
Good work. You were a great queen.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:02.710
True to form, huh?

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:05.000
Shut up! I don't want to hear it!

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.170
Good job out there.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:06.630
Yeah!

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:09.880
Well, everyone ready for the climax?

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:20.130
I love you, even if Heaven 
and Earth should fall!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.690
Oh, this is the kiss scene, isn't it?

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:24.300
Think they'll actually do it?

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:32.700
Nah, I guess they wouldn't 
do that for real.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.150
Yeah, I guess not.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:47.750
Hime! Nozomi!

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:19.990
Thanks.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:39.880
The crowd loved it. 
I'd say it went perfect!

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:43.180
It seems it's causing some 
trouble now, though.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.270
Yeah, one wrong move and you guys
 would've been seriously hurt.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:51.190
Well, the class president 
will take care of all that.

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:55.400
You guys were great!

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.240
Thank you, thank you!

00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:59.820
What's wrong with you?

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:01.660
Don't be all bashful.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.120
You're gonna make <i>me</i> embarrassed.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.660
But...

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:06.500
At least you two are enjoying yourselves.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:09.630
What? Want me to kiss you, too?

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:10.460
No need!

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:17.010
<b>#1 
A Part</b>

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:17.010
<b>When All Is Said
 And Done, 
Everyone Loves 
Kisses.</b>

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:51.980
<b>Did You Know That a Marathon 
Is a Microcosm of Life?</b>

00:11:53.730 --> 00:12:00.610
Modern mammals, birds, reptiles, 
and amphibians have six legs.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:04.780
It's believed that this 
originated with fish,

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:11.000
<b>The Origin of Humans</b>

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:10.750
whose pectoral, front ventral, 
and rear ventral fins became legs.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:14.040
The genes that determined the 
shape of the pectoral fins

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.090
duplicated to form ventral fins,

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:19.510
which duplicated again to 
form rear ventral fins.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:24.470
Of course, in prehistoric times 
there were also four-legged amphibians,

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:27.430
but they died out and left 
no surviving descendants.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:27.890
<b>Extinct</b>

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:30.680
It's likely that, to support such 
large bodies on such weak legs,

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:33.890
six legs were more advantageous than four.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:38.020
Humans, the ultimate product of evolution,

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:41.340
can be broadly divided into 
the following four groups.

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:47.950
<b>Catfolk
Fauns</b>

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:48.160
The first group includes the 
catfolk, goatfolk, and fauns.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:52.410
<b>Angelfolk</b>

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:52.580
The next includes the 
angelfolk and draconids.

00:12:52.660 --> 00:13:01.300
<b>Centaurs</b>

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:55.330
Third, the centaurs.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:59.290
Weretigers also used to be 
included in this group,

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:01.350
but they are now extinct.

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:06.680
<b>Merfolk</b>

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:05.840
Finally, while none of the students 
in this room are part of this group,

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:07.140
there's the merfolk.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:13.680
In the past, the vast differences 
in appearance between these groups

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.560
led to many wars and 
abundant discrimination.

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:19.340
If the four-legged amphibians had survived,

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:22.940
become the dominant race, 
and evolved into humans...

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:30.870
At most they might have had different 
hair, skin, and eye colors,

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:34.040
but serious discrimination 
would have been unlikely.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:39.130
But the idea of a world where 
humans have four limbs

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:41.380
is no more than a fantasy.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:45.470
In our world, a single misstep

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:48.970
carries the danger of easily landing 
us in a hellish situation.

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:52.810
Whether we become a world at war,
 like the lesser nations,

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.590
or a peaceful world that 
has attained harmony

00:13:56.230 --> 00:14:01.110
depends on whether we can all 
come together in equal unity.

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:04.990
Therefore, equality is often more valuable

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:07.910
than civil rights, and even life itself!

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.250
Now, we'll conclude with the 
singing of the national anthem.

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.040
Yes, ma'am.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:17.920
Stand.

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:38.230
W-Wait...

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:46.490
You're so slow.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:49.910
Run... slower...

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:52.490
You're like this after only two kilometers?

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.830
You really don't exercise enough, Kyoko.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.750
That's easy for you to say.

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:04.750
In the first place, how is it fair that 
we all have to run the same distance?

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:09.010
I go running with my mom every day.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.470
We do about twenty kilometers.

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:13.470
What for? To lose weight?

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:16.020
Well...

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:18.350
You don't look that fat to me, though.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:23.940
When centaurs get too heavy, 
we can't turn our bodies normally,

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:25.600
so we can't even wipe our own behinds.

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:28.990
Wait, you can actually wipe your own?

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:31.740
Of course I can!

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:34.160
Jeez!

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:37.240
Wait, I said...

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:46.000
Kyoko, you'd better get in shape,
or you won't be able to wipe your butt.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:47.210
Not gonna happen!

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:50.300
You never gain weight, 
no matter how much you eat, do you?

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.000
Y-Yeah, I guess.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.640
You're so lucky.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:57.890
Wh-What? What was that laugh for?

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:01.600
Well, Kyoko, you're just 
perfectly straight up and down.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.050
That's nothing to be jealous of.

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:06.110
I oughta slug you!

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:08.940
Try to catch me, then!

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:11.900
You little...! Stop! Hey!

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:12.610
This way!

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:13.450
Wait!

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.620
Hey, you're running pretty fast.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:17.790
Wait...

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:21.870
I can't...

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:26.540
Are you okay?

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.550
Jeez, don't kill yourself.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:30.710
Whose fault do you think this is?

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:38.680
What now? Do you want me to carry you?

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:41.350
No, no, that's a bad idea.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:44.730
I'd be accused of discrimination
 and sent to a correctional clinic.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.820
That's a bit dramatic...

00:16:47.820 --> 00:16:49.860
No, it's not.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:53.740
In this country,
 centaurs were once warriors,

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:56.820
but in some countries they were basically 
slaves that people used as mounts.

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:58.830
So they crack down on that stuff.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:01.330
That's where most modern 
laws originated, you know.

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:06.080
Of course, just talking like 
this is illegal, but still...

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:09.550
Well, once you've caught your breath, 
let's take our time finishing.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:12.380
It's okay. You can go on ahead.

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:18.100
It's not like we're gunning 
for first place or anything.

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:20.760
I bet Tama-chan is trying for that, though.

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:23.310
Yeah, that's what the class 
president loves most of all.

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:29.150
Well, if there were prize money, 
I'd totally leave you behind.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:33.110
Okay, let's go.

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:34.660
Huh? Already?

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:37.650
We won't make it back 
to the school in time.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.190
Come on!

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.040
Let's get moving!

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:45.080
Let's take our time, okay?

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:58.590
Hey...

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:03.180
Hime, how fast can you run 
when you actually try?

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.430
Hmm...

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:08.190
I can run 100 meters in about nine seconds?

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.060
Is that fast?

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:11.570
It's super fast!

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:13.820
Why don't I run for a bit?

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:16.860
There are no cars coming,
so I'll run to the stoplight.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:18.950
Hey, be careful, will you?

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:21.530
Okay, ready... Go!

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:24.440
She's fast!

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:26.830
Wait, is she gonna be able to stop?

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.700
Hime! Stop, stop!

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:49.310
Hey! What are you thinking?!

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.440
I'm sorry!

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:55.730
Hime!

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:58.150
Are you okay?

00:18:58.150 --> 00:18:59.070
Yeah.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:02.240
Jeez...

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:04.540
You really are fast!

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:08.120
If you joined the track club, 
you'd kick butt!

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:14.750
I've been told that before,
 so I tried joining once, but...

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:16.170
Set!

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:18.380
H-Huh?

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:20.220
Huh?!

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:24.220
Yeah, the tracks are divided up by race.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.010
Yeah.

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:28.020
But wouldn't ball sports, 
like basketball, be the same?

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.260
Here! Pass!

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:38.940
Hime has horsepower, 
but she's kind of a klutz.

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:42.610
What a waste.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:46.160
Still, just being faster than 
most people must be nice.

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:49.080
You're just way too out of shape, Kyoko.

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:52.000
How long are you gonna lean on me, anyway?

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:54.840
Come on, let's go.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:56.340
Sorry.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:03.760
Hey, you three! Take this more seriously!

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.640
Lunch break is about to end!

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:06.680
Okay!

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:08.510
Wait, is that...?

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:13.650
What are you doing there?

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:18.900
Oh, well... Running a marathon after 
being up all night was too much.

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.900
Which means we're already over capacity,

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:23.700
so try your best to finish, Kyoko-chan!

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.320
Huh?!

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:27.280
You heard her. Get moving!

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:29.200
See ya!

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:30.160
Bye.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:37.170
Don't get discouraged! Come on!

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:39.760
Huh?

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:42.680
Nozomi-chan, that's the wrong way!

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:47.180
The patrol's already gone past us,
 so let's take a shortcut.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:49.640
That's an unusually good idea from you.

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:51.480
You're one to talk!

00:20:53.190 --> 00:20:54.730
Is this really okay?

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:58.440
This is still...

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:00.400
pretty far...

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:03.940
That's what happens when you slack off 
all the time and never exercise.

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:06.410
We're almost at the goal!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:09.700
You're finally here.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:12.040
Afternoon classes are starting.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:17.170
